<title>JAPAN: Japan Jan rubber imports up 4.3 pct yr/yr - MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan Jan rubber imports up 4.3 pct yr/yr - MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's rubber imports in January totalled 63,921 tonnes, up 4.3 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Friday showed.</p>
<p>Figures were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			Jan 97	 Dec 96	Jan 96</p>
<p> Total		63,921	 52,519	61,285</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Thailand	   44,668	 34,482	44,369</p>
<p> Indonesia	  13,819	 12,467	11,410</p>
<p> Malaysia	    4,025	  4,210	 3,651</p>
<p>Imports in 1996 were 713,792 tonnes, up 4.0 percent from 686,449 tonnes in a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
</text>
